% C8-WHAT: WHAT (RDEF:1419) NAMES THE WORD WHOSE CODE HOLDS AN ADDRESS.
% EXAMINE_ENTRY (RDEF:1405) ACCEPTS FROM THE FIRST BYTE OF THE CODE
% THROUGH THE BYTE AFTER IT, NEWEST WORD FIRST.  SO THE START OF A WORD
% IS ITSELF, THE BYTE BEFORE IS THE WORD BEFORE, AND CODE_PNTR IS THE
% NEWEST WORD.  ADDRESSES DEPEND ON THE BUILD.
DECIMAL
'W0 : 0 ;
'W1 : 1 ;
'W2 : 2 2 + ;
"W1      " MSG () W1 WHAT CR
"W1+1    " MSG () W1 1+ WHAT CR
"W1-1    " MSG () W1 1- WHAT CR
"W2-1    " MSG () W2 1- WHAT CR
"W2      " MSG () W2 WHAT CR
"PNTR-1  " MSG CODE_PNTR @ 1- WHAT CR
"PNTR    " MSG CODE_PNTR @ WHAT CR
"ZERO    " MSG 0 WHAT CR
"WHERE   " MSG 'W2 WHERE CR 'NOSUCHWORD WHERE CR
"AFTER   " MSG 12345 = CR
